  "rationale": "Each test checks a property that any correct solution must satisfy, derived directly from the specification. The tests verify: the output contains only names from input, no duplicates, order matches last occurrence indices, each input name appears exactly once in output, output lines are valid names, counts match unique names, first output equals last input name if unique, output preserves relative order of last occurrences, and a brute-force simulation for small inputs (n ≤ 20). The weakest test is the 'last_is_first' because it assumes a specific mapping condition that may not always hold (though it does per spec). If I had to drop one first, it would be that one.",
