{
  "rationale": "The tests are based on the specification's constraints and the mathematical definition of change when paying with 1000-yen bills: change = (ceil(N/1000)*1000) - N. Instead of computing the exact answer, each test checks a necessary property of the output: it must be an integer between 0 and 999 inclusive, it must satisfy (N + change) % 1000 == 0, and it must not exceed 1000. Also, for small inputs (N ≤ 1000) we can compute the exact change by brute force (since N ≤ 10000, the brute force is still fast). One test also verifies the output format is a single integer followed by a newline. The weakest test is `test_change_not_negative` because it's implied by the stronger `test_change_range`, but it's kept for clarity. The first to drop would be `test_change_not_negative`.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_output_format",
      "source": "def test_output_format(run, x):\n    output = run(x)\n    # Should be a single integer, possibly with a newline\n    lines = output.strip().split('\\n')\n    assert len(lines) == 1, 'Output should be exactly one line'\n    value = lines[0]\n    # Must be an integer\n    int(value)  # Raises ValueError if not integer"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_change_range",
      "source": "def test_change_range(run, x):\n    N = int(x.strip())\n    change = int(run(x).strip())\n    # Change must be 0 <= change <= 999\n    assert 0 <= change <= 999, f'Change {change} out of valid range [0,999] for N={N}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_change_non_negative",
      "source": "def test_change_non_negative(run, x):\n    change = int(run(x).strip())\n    assert change >= 0, 'Change cannot be negative'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_change_mod_1000",
      "source": "def test_change_mod_1000(run, x):\n    N = int(x.strip())\n    change = int(run(x).strip())\n    # (N + change) must be a multiple of 1000\n    assert (N + change) % 1000 == 0, f'N+change={N+change} not divisible by 1000'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_change_less_than_1000",
      "source": "def test_change_less_than_1000(run, x):\n    change = int(run(x).strip())\n    assert change < 1000, 'Change must be less than 1000'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_exact_for_small_N",
      "source": "def test_exact_for_small_N(run, x):\n    N = int(x.strip())\n    if N <= 1000:\n        # We can brute force the minimal k such that k*1000 >= N\n        k = (N + 999) // 1000  # ceil division\n        expected = k * 1000 - N\n        change = int(run(x).strip())\n        assert change == expected, f'For N={N} expected {expected}, got {change}'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_change_integer",
      "source": "def test_change_integer(run, x):\n    output = run(x).strip()\n    # Already checked in format test, but double-check\n    try:\n        int(output)\n    except ValueError:\n        assert False, 'Change must be an integer'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_change_not_exceeding_1000",
      "source": "def test_change_not_exceeding_1000(run, x):\n    N = int(x.strip())\n    change = int(run(x).strip())\n    # Since we pay with at least ceil(N/1000) bills, change <= 1000-1\n    # But also, if N is a multiple of 1000, change is 0.\n    # So we just enforce change <= 1000 (allowing 1000 would be wrong).\n    assert change <= 1000, f'Change {change} exceeds 1000'"
    },
